Chapter: HelperBuffersArm
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceEffect

 The negative arm for one helper called twice in one kernel with different
 buffers. `run.ps1` must exit 6 and name
 `CODEX_REFUSED_helper_called_with_two_buffer_mappings`: the module-scope
 buffers a helper reads are fixed per kernel, so the second call would read
 the first call's buffers.

 We say:

Section: Kernel

  hb-dot : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Real
  hb-dot (a) (b) (i) = act
    x <- device-load-f32 a i
    y <- device-load-f32 b i
    x * y
  end

  hb-step : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  hb-step (xb) (yb) (zb) (wb) (outb) (gid) = act
    p <- hb-dot xb yb gid
    q <- hb-dot zb wb gid
    device-store-f32 outb gid (p + q)
  end

